<div class="instruction">
<strong>INVESTIGATOR INSTRUCTION:</strong>
Examine each exhibit separately before deciding how the pieces connect. Add confirmed times to your case timeline and record any questions raised by the evidence.
</div>

<div class="section-heading">
<small>Evidence Set 01</small>
<h2>Documentary Evidence</h2>
</div>

<section class="exhibit-grid">

<!-- EXHIBIT A -->
<article class="exhibit">
<div class="exhibit-head">
<strong>Community Centre Floor Plan</strong>
<span class="exhibit-label">Exhibit A</span>
</div>
<div class="exhibit-body">

<p>This simplified plan shows the rooms relevant to Friday evening's investigation.</p>

<div class="floorplan">
<div class="room office">Office<br><small>Computer + filing cabinet</small><span class="camera">CCTV A</span></div>
<div class="room meeting">Youth Meeting Room</div>
<div class="room store">Storage / Cleaner Area</div>
<div class="room entry">Main Entry / Hall<span class="camera">CCTV B</span></div>
</div>

<div class="note"><strong>Known:</strong> The office computer could access the association's online banking. The office was not locked during the youth meeting.</div>

<details>
<summary>Investigator prompts</summary>
<div class="find"><strong>Find it:</strong> Which rooms would a person need to pass through to reach the office?</div>
<div class="question"><strong>Question it:</strong> Does being near the office prove that a person used the computer? Explain.</div>
</details>

</div>
</article>

<!-- EXHIBIT B -->
<article class="exhibit">
<div class="exhibit-head">
<strong>Friday CCTV / Access Log</strong>
<span class="exhibit-label">Exhibit B</span>
</div>
<div class="exhibit-body">

<table class="log">
<tr><th>Time</th><th>Observation</th></tr>
<tr><td>4:47 pm</td><td>Claire Bennett enters through the main doors.</td></tr>
<tr><td>5:03 pm</td><td>Alex Morgan enters.</td></tr>
<tr><td>5:07 pm</td><td>Mia Tran enters.</td></tr>
<tr><td>5:21 pm</td><td>Councillor Daniel Reed enters.</td></tr>
<tr><td>5:43 pm</td><td>Mia Tran leaves the meeting room and walks toward the main hall.</td></tr>
<tr><td>5:48 pm</td><td>Alex Morgan leaves the building.</td></tr>
<tr><td>5:54 pm</td><td>Daniel Reed leaves the building.</td></tr>
<tr><td>6:12 pm</td><td>Claire Bennett leaves.</td></tr>
<tr><td>6:18 pm</td><td>Sam Patel locks the main entrance.</td></tr>
</table>

<div class="note"><strong>Important:</strong> CCTV A records the office doorway, but footage from 5:25–5:45 pm is unavailable due to a recording fault.</div>

<details>
<summary>Investigator prompts</summary>
<div class="find"><strong>Add to timeline:</strong> Record each confirmed arrival and departure.</div>
<div class="question"><strong>Connect it:</strong> Who was definitely inside the building at 5:36 pm?</div>
</details>

</div>
</article>

<!-- EXHIBIT C -->
<article class="exhibit">
<div class="exhibit-head">
<strong>Bank Transaction Record</strong>
<span class="exhibit-label">Exhibit C</span>
</div>
<div class="exhibit-body">

<div class="bank">
<div class="bank-top">
<strong>Banksia Creek Community Association</strong>
<span>Project Account •••• 7314</span>
</div>

<div class="bank-row head">
<div>Date / Time</div><div>Description</div><div>Amount</div><div>Balance</div>
</div>

<div class="bank-row">
<div>4 Sep<br>4:10 pm</div><div>Opening balance</div><div>—</div><div>$18,993.16</div>
</div>

<div class="bank-row">
<div>4 Sep<br>5:36 pm</div><div>Online transfer<br>Ref: BC RESERVE</div><div class="negative">−$18,750.00</div><div>$243.16</div>
</div>

<div class="bank-row">
<div>7 Sep<br>8:03 am</div><div>Balance enquiry</div><div>—</div><div>$243.16</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="note"><strong>Confirmed:</strong> The transfer occurred at <strong>5:36 pm Friday</strong>.</div>

<details>
<summary>Investigator prompts</summary>
<div class="find"><strong>Add to timeline:</strong> 5:36 pm — $18,750 electronically transferred.</div>
<div class="question"><strong>Judge it:</strong> Does this document show who authorised the transfer? What does it prove — and what does it not prove?</div>
</details>

</div>
</article>

<!-- EXHIBIT D -->
<article class="exhibit">
<div class="exhibit-head">
<strong>Youth Committee Meeting Record</strong>
<span class="exhibit-label">Exhibit D</span>
</div>
<div class="exhibit-body">

<div class="minutes">
<h3>Banksia Creek Youth Recreation Committee</h3>
<p><strong>Friday, 4 September 2026</strong><br>
Meeting scheduled: 5:00–5:45 pm</p>

<p><strong>Present:</strong> Alex Morgan, Mia Tran, Claire Bennett (first 15 minutes), three other youth committee members.</p>

<ul>
<li>Discussed equipment ideas for the recreation area.</li>
<li>Alex raised concerns that council delays could increase building costs.</li>
<li>Claire left the meeting at approximately 5:15 pm to complete association paperwork.</li>
<li>Meeting finished at approximately 5:45 pm.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="note"><strong>Context:</strong> Alex had publicly supported the project. Councillor Reed had previously questioned whether council should support it.</div>

<details>
<summary>Investigator prompts</summary>
<div class="question"><strong>Think:</strong> Does disagreement about the project create motive? Is motive the same as proof?</div>
</details>

</div>
</article>

<!-- EXHIBIT E -->
<article class="exhibit">
<div class="exhibit-head">
<strong>Email Received by Treasurer</strong>
<span class="exhibit-label">Exhibit E</span>
</div>
<div class="exhibit-body">

<div class="email">
<div class="email-line"><strong>From:</strong> CommunityBank Security &lt;security-alert@communitybank-support.net&gt;</div>
<div class="email-line"><strong>To:</strong> Claire Bennett</div>
<div class="email-line"><strong>Sent:</strong> Friday, 4 September 2026 — 4:58 pm</div>
<div class="email-line"><strong>Subject:</strong> URGENT SECURITY ACTION REQUIRED</div>

<div class="email-body">
<p>Dear Account Holder,</p>

<p>Unusual activity has been detected on your community organisation account.</p>

<p>To prevent loss of project funds, immediately move the balance to the secure reserve account supplied through the security portal. The funds will remain protected while our team completes verification.</p>

<p><strong>Action must be completed before 6:00 pm today.</strong></p>

<p>Failure to act may result in account suspension.</p>

<p>CommunityBank Account Security</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="flag"><strong>Possible warning signs:</strong> unusual sender domain • urgent language • request to move money • generic greeting</div>

<details>
<summary>Investigator prompts</summary>
<div class="find"><strong>Add to timeline:</strong> 4:58 pm — suspicious security email received.</div>
<div class="question"><strong>Connect it:</strong> How could this email change your interpretation of the bank transfer?</div>
</details>

</div>
</article>

<!-- EXHIBIT F -->
<article class="exhibit">
<div class="exhibit-head">
<strong>Text Message Extract</strong>
<span class="exhibit-label">Exhibit F</span>
</div>
<div class="exhibit-body">

<p>Extract recovered from a message exchange between Mia Tran and Alex Morgan on Friday evening.</p>

<div class="phone">
<div class="screen">

<div class="bubble left">
<strong>Mia — 5:49 pm</strong><br>
Did you leave already?
</div>

<div class="bubble right">
<strong>Alex — 5:50 pm</strong><br>
Yeah. Heading home. Mum's picking me up near the oval.
</div>

<div class="bubble left">
<strong>Mia — 5:51 pm</strong><br>
Claire looked stressed when she came back past the hall.
</div>

<div class="bubble right">
<strong>Alex — 5:52 pm</strong><br>
Probably more council paperwork lol
</div>

<div class="bubble left">
<strong>Mia — 5:53 pm</strong><br>
Reed was still arguing about the project earlier.
</div>

</div>
</div>

<div class="note"><strong>Remember:</strong> A text message may show what somebody believed at the time. It does not automatically prove that belief was correct.</div>

<details>
<summary>Investigator prompts</summary>
<div class="question"><strong>Check it:</strong> Which parts of these messages are supported by other exhibits? Which parts are opinion?</div>
</details>

</div>
</article>

</section>

<section class="taskbox">
<h2>Evidence Locker Task</h2>
<p>Before opening the witness statements, update your investigation notes.</p>

<div class="task-grid">

<div class="task-mini">
<strong>1. Timeline</strong>
<p>Add every confirmed time from Exhibits B, C, D, E and F.</p>
</div>

<div class="task-mini">
<strong>2. Strongest Evidence</strong>
<p>Choose the three exhibits you currently think are most important. Explain why.</p>
</div>

<div class="task-mini">
<strong>3. Theory Check</strong>
<p>Rewrite your current theory. What has changed since the Case Brief?</p>
</div>

</div>

<p><strong>Do not decide guilt yet.</strong> The next stage contains witness statements that may support, challenge or contradict the documentary evidence.</p>
</section>

